        "actionType": {
          "value": "reaction"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A damaging effect hits two or more targets, at least one of which is a tentacle.</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> One of the affected tentacles absorbs the damage into itself. The affected tentacle gets a result one degree of success worse against the save, or an attack gets an additional degree of success against it.</p><p>Targets other than that tentacle gain an additional degree of success against the save, or attacks against them get a result one degree of success worse.</p><p>For the purpose of chain lightning, as this reaction can only be triggered if the first tentacle does not critically succeed, when used treat it as the reaction being used on the first tentacle (i.e. reduce the degree of success of the first target by one, then increase the degree of success of all future saves against the spell) to avoid retroactive critical successes ending the spell.</p><p>In Tier 5, Scylladon gains an additional reaction that can only be used for Tentacular Absorption. If an effect would prevent Scylladon from gaining or using reactions, it only applies to the extra reaction granted by Tentacular Absorption.</p>"
        },
